# Tailwind, not inline styles

Style UI with Tailwind `className`, including Remotion components (`Img`, `Interactive.*`, `AbsoluteFill`). Do not use `style={{ ... }}` for layout, typography, color, overflow, or other static CSS.

Merge classes with `cn()` from `src/lib/utils.ts`. Never concatenate `className` strings.

```tsx
import { cn } from "../lib/utils";

// ❌ BAD
<Interactive.Div style={{ opacity: 0.9, fontWeight: 500 }}>{songName}</Interactive.Div>
<Img style={{ width: "100%", height: "100%", objectFit: "cover" }} src={src} />
<div className={`min-w-0 truncate ${className ?? ""}`} />

// ✅ GOOD
<Interactive.Div className="truncate font-medium opacity-90">{songName}</Interactive.Div>
<Img className="size-full object-cover" src={src} />
<div className={cn("min-w-0 truncate", className)} />
```

The only exception to Tailwind is values it cannot express as a class: per-frame `interpolate()` animation, and a third-party CSS variable that has no class equivalent.
